to fight  demons and save innocent people oh and  back to the marriage question becoming a  demon sire meant that mitsuri would be  around a lot of extremely strong men so  she could finally find a man to marry  who was stronger than her so he wouldn't  be intimidated by her own strength this  plan didn't work out so well though  because mitsuri quickly advanced through  the demonstranks and became a hashira  this meant that even within the demon  slayers very few men were actually  stronger than her before she became a  hashira mitsuri was trained by kyojiro  renkoku she learned his flame breathing  style of swordsmanship but she later  modified it into her own custom style  known as love breathing love breathing  is unique because it takes full  advantage of mitsuri's special physique  including her superhuman flexibility and  incredible muscle density in the rengoku  gaiden chapters we get a glimpse of  renkoku training mitsuri and we even get  to see the moment mitsuri gets her first  official demon slayer uniform and yes it  is definitely a perfectly normal  regulation demon slayer uniform soon  after that all the hashira are summoned  by oyakatasama by this point kyojo  rengoku's father shinjuro had already  given up on being a hashira after the  death of his wife he began drinking  heavily and he lost the will to fight as  a result he refuses to answer oya  katasama's summons for all the hashira  and so kyojiro renkoku decides to go  instead of his father despite the fact  that he is still not the flame hashira  at this point in time after rengoku  expresses his desire to become the next  flame hashira at the hashira meeting  oyakatasama gives him the opportunity to  prove himself worthy by defeating lower  moon to heidel a demon who has been  threatening the capital city of tokyo  rengoku takes mitsuri on this mission  with him and this is the first mission  that they ever go on together mitsuri is  able to learn a lot from rangoku during  this battle not just in terms of  fighting but also in terms of character  rengoku is also an outcast as far as  social expectations go he also has  extremely unusual hair his clothes are  unconventional he carries a sword  everywhere he goes and so on since they  have to travel to tokyo which is full of  people rengoku gets quite a few comments  about being strange and weird and scary  but he just brushes them off in stride  and continues to smile and to do his job  this inspires mitsuri to follow in  rengoku's footsteps it is during the  fight against lower moon 2 heido that  mitsuri begins to develop her own unique  breathing style the breath of love which  was of course greatly inspired by  rengoku's flame breathing ultimately  haidou falls after an epic battle  against the burning determination of  rengoku and as a result kyojiro replaces  his father shinjuro as the flame hashira  meanwhile mitsuri has finally found a  place where she can be herself and  people that accept her for who she is  this allows her to tap into her full  potential and eventually she too becomes  a hashira since we just talked about  mitsuri let's talk about the man who is  clearly in love with her the serpent  hashira obanai iguro just like mitsuri  iguro carries a lot of personal baggage  and he has serious confidence issues in  fact he feels that he isn't worthy of  mitsuri because his bloodline is corrupt  and impure for centuries his family only  seemed to be giving birth to girls and  iguru appeared to have been the only boy  who was born into the family in like 370  years once he was born he was confined  to a prison cell where he was fond over  by his mother sisters and aunts and  brought rich foods to eat every single  day igor eventually learned that his  entire family worshipped a female demon  who was half human and half snake and he  also learned that they had been feeding  their own offspring to this demon as  sacrifices in return the demon made the  family rich by giving them the valuables  of all the other humans that she killed  because igura was born with unusual eyes  the snake demon took a liking to him and  she decided that she wouldn't eat him as  a baby instead she apparently decided  that she would wait until he was older  and fatten him up she also had his mouth  sliced so that it would more closely  resemble her own snake mouth thankfully  before he could be eaten igor managed to  escape his cell and run away the snake  demon tried to capture him but she was  killed by the former flame hashira  shinjuro rengoku who at the time was the  current flame hashira before she was  killed the snake demon took out nearly  everyone in iguoda's large family  because they failed to prevent his  escape and so igoro continued to carry  the burden of his family's sins as well  as the death of most of his family  members for his entire life he had  decided long ago that he wanted to die  defeating muzon in order to purify the  filthy blood of his family and so he  trained hard to become a demon slayer  and a hashira even though deep down he  considered himself to be weak and  unworthy but if he were to be one day  reborn as a human in a peaceful world  without demons he would then finally  confess his true feelings for mitsuri  there are a ton of interesting buddhist  and hinduist influences to igoro's  backstory including the idea of  purifying oneself karma and being  reincarnated into a better life but i  don't want to get too deeply into that  because this is already going to be a  very long video the important thing to  take away from all of this is that just  like mitsuri igor always thought of  himself as an outcast who would never be  accepted by society part of it was  because of his unconventional upbringing  part of it was the sins of his bloodline  and part of it was his physical  appearance because his face had been  scarred by the snake demon and of course  he also had those unique eyes and yet  within the demon slayer core iguru found  a place to belong he found people who  accepted him and he even found love the  demon slayers were able to recognize  true talent and potential in people who  were rejected and looked down upon by  society and that is in no small part due  to how kind compassionate and  open-minded oya katasama is  next up let's talk about the star of the  entertainment district arc the gigachad  tengen uzui tangen comes from ashinobi  or ninja family and he was one of nine  siblings his family was extremely  committed to the shinobi way of life and  three of his siblings died before they  even reached the age of 10 due to the  extreme ninja training methods that they  were put through and that is not even  the worst part the remaining six  siblings including tengan were  essentially forced to fight each other  to the death by their own father  apparently all of the siblings were made  to wear masks during the fight so they  didn't even know whom they were fighting  tan tangent only realized what was  really going on after he had already  killed two of his own brothers in the  end only tangent and one other brother  survived and while tengan's last  surviving brother accepted their  father's belief that ginobi must be  willing to commit even the harshest acts  in order to protect their clan tangent  simply could not accept this horrible  mindset he decided to abandon his clan  and he left the shinobi village of his  birth along with his three hot ninja  wives you see the uzui family practiced  polygamy and so tengen was forced to go  through an arranged marriage with three  kunuichi women who were chosen by the  head of their shinobi clan after they  left their clan tengen encouraged his  wives to completely reevaluate their  most fundamental values from a very  young age shinobi are taught to place  their clan and their mission above all  other things including their own lives  if a shinobi must sacrifice their life  in order to complete a mission then so  be it that should be considered an honor  however after abandoning his clan tangan  also abandoned those values he  encouraged his wives to value themselves  and their own lives over any mission  which proves that tangan really cares  about his wives and that he values the  sanctity of human life over clan  loyalties he even considered  exterminating his former clan in order  to prevent them from committing more  evil deeds but in the end he just  couldn't bring himself to go through  with killing his own father and brother  after leaving the uzui clan tangent met  oyakatasama and he joined the demon  player corps he climbed the ranks of the  organization until he eventually became  the sound hashira tangen has an immense  amount of respect for oya katasama and  he would be happy to lay down his own  life for the leader of the demon slayers  tangent is such an interesting character  because despite abandoning his clan  which is the biggest sin and the  greatest dishonor for ashinobi he  remained a valiant and honorable man but  he has a completely different code of  honor from his father and brother  instead of valuing his clan above  everything else and trying to make the  clan stronger by any means necessary  tengen values justice and protecting the  innocent he would happily give up his  own life for a noble cause like that one  but he will not fight for a cause that  he doesn't believe in just because that  is what's expected of him by tradition  and the society he grew up in despite  the fact that he is likely considered to  be a traitor and a coward by his clan  members he is actually a truly honorable  and brave warrior for tengen real honor  and real bravery is fighting for a just  cause and he believes that the demon  stairs have the most just cause of all  protecting the innocent from vicious  demons  now let's talk about the insect hashira  shinobu kocho shinobu had an older  sister named kanai and they were both  raised in a loving home by their parents  according to the second demonstrator  fanbook her parents worked in  compounding medicine which i think means  that they mixed medical ingredients  together to create specific medicines  for individual people unfortunately one  day their parents were killed by a demon  this same demon was about to kill  shinobu and kana as well but thankfully  they were rescued by the stone hashira  gyome himejima the tragic loss of their  parents had a profound effect on the two  sisters and they both vowed to become  demons players just like the man who  rescued them they both wanted to become  stronger so that they could protect each  other and so they could spare other  families from suffering the same fate as  their family  kanai eventually became the flower  hashira and shinobu stuck close to her  sister and learned a lot from her one  day while traveling kanai and chinobu  came across a little girl that was being  treated like a slave they freed the girl  from her captor and took her back to the  butterfly mansion where they essentially  adopted her they named the girl kanal  and this is of course the same kanaoh  who is shinobu's current tsuguko or  apprentice some years later when shinobu  was 14 and kanai was 17 kane engaged in  battle against upper moon 2 doma kanae  was mortally wounded during this battle  but doma couldn't finish her off because  the sun was about to come out and so he  decided to flee in chapter 141 we get a  quick flashback to khanna's death and we  see that chinobu arrived on the scene in  time to say goodbye to her sister before  she passes away kannada tells shinobu to  leave the demons air corps so she could  grow old and be happy and so she could  just live out a normal life but shinobu  refuses to quit and instead she vows to  avenge her sister by killing the demon  who killed her after kana's death  shinobu succeeds her sister as the  master of the butterfly estate from that  point forward shinobu becomes even more  determined to destroy the demons and  especially upper moon to doma upon  meeting shinobu tanjiro can tell that  something is off about her otherwise  calm demeanor he can tell that she is  hiding a lot of anger inside of her  tanjiro is indeed correct shinobu has  always been angry her parents were  killed by demons her older sister was  killed by demons and all her apprentices  except for kanel were also killed by  demons these demons killed so many  innocent people they destroyed so many  families and chinobu has been absolutely  furious about it for a very long time  this fury is what drives her to seek  justice at all costs  next up let's talk about shinobu's  savior and the strongest hashira the  stone pillar gyome himejima before he  became a demon slayer gyome was a blind  monk who raised the nine orphans inside  a temple although they didn't have much  they took care of each other and lived  together as a family but one night one  of the children broke the rules of the  temple and didn't return home before  dark that child was captured by a demon  in the forest and was about to be eaten  in order to save himself he made a deal  with the demon if the demon spares his  life he will lead him to the other eight  children at the temple since this area  was known for demon activity gyome had  taken precautions and he burned wisteria  flower incense every night to keep the  demons away  but the orphan who made the deal with  the demon extinguished the incense so  that the demon would be able to enter  the temple four of the children were  taken out instantly and gyome tried to  protect the other four but since he was  blind and not nearly as strong as he is  now three of the children ran off on  their own instead of hiding behind him  and unfortunately those three children  fell victim to the demon when the demon  finally came for gyomei and the final  child gyome decided that he had to fight  back despite being a monk who hated  violence he began fighting the demon  with his bare hands and he just kept on  punching him like a madman until the sun  came out and the demon was killed the  big scar on gyome's forehead came from  this fight against a demon now again  because most people didn't believe in  demons and since the demon's body  disintegrated once the sun came out when  the last surviving child who was only 4  years old tried to explain the situation  to the authorities they thought the  child was telling them that gyome went  crazy and killed all the children so  despite being the one who defeated the  demon and protected the last surviving  child gyome was arrested for murder he  was going to be executed but thankfully  oyakatasama was able to rescue him and  he recruited him into the demon slayer  core since then gyome has been training  relentlessly and he has achieved peak  physical condition he has developed his  physical body to the highest possible  extent and that is why he has earned the  title of the strongest hashira now let's  talk about the youngest hashira the 14  year old missed hashira muichiro tokito  muichiro had a twin brother named  yuichiro and their father was a humble  woodcutter at age 10 they lost their  mother to pneumonia and they tragically  lost their father around the same time  he had actually gone to pick medicinal  herbs for their sick mother during a  storm and he slipped and fell off a  cliff the two 10 year old twins then  suddenly found themselves living alone  as orphans yuichiro was the slightly  older brother and he developed a cynical  outlook on life he thought that their  father was foolish to go out in that  storm in an attempt to help their mother  by that point her condition was already  too severe for some herbs to help her  and if their father had just stayed home  that night then only their mother would  have died instead of both of them  muichiro was more compassionate and  sentimental and he disagreed with his  brother's outlook on life  the following year when the brothers  were around 11 oya katasama's wife came  to visit them at their home she told  them that they were descendants of  legendary swordsmen and that one of  their ancestors was the original breath  of the sun user she wanted the two of  them to become demon slayers but  yuichiro turned her away he did not want  them to risk their own lives trying to  help others because if they did that  then they would just end up like their  father yuichiro simply did not trust the  demonstrators or anyone else and he  refused to foolishly risk his own life  then one night a demon found their home  and attacked them yuichiro was severely  injured and suddenly muichiro snapped he  used his woodcutting axes and every  other tool at his disposal to cut up the  demon and keep him that way until the  sun came out and killed him when he  finally returned to the house muichiro  found his brother praying to the gods  and buddhas to spare muichiro's life  because unlike yuichiro muichiro had a  kind heart and he wanted to help others  yuichiro would ultimately die in his  brother's arms eventually oyakatasama's  wife returned and she was able to heal  muichiro and save his life muichiro then  joined the demonstra corps and the  trauma he experienced blocked out most  memories that he had of his former life  due to his legendary lineage and his  incredible talent muichiro quickly rose  through the ranks of the demonstrators  and he became akhashira only two months  after joining the demon slayer core it  is hard to even imagine what an insane  achievement that is due to the mix of  trauma and memory loss that muichiro  experienced his personality began to  resemble that of his older brother  yuichiro instead of his usual  compassionate and idealistic self he  became more cold and distant he also  felt a deep-seated anger towards the  demons and this anger motivated him to  keep doing his best to hunt them all  down finally let's talk about the wind  hashira sanemi shinazugawa sunemi was  the eldest of seven children which  included his younger brother genya their  father was abusive to his wife and his  children and his mother would often  sacrifice herself in order to shield her  children from her husband's attacks one  day sanemi's father died after being  stabbed by someone he had gotten into a  fight with and sonomy didn't even feel  sorry for his father he felt that his  father got exactly what he deserved  after their father's death sanemy and  genya tried to take responsibility for  taking care of their family since their  mother was kind and compassionate things  seemed to be going well for a while but  then as is so often the case with  demonstrator another tragedy struck one  day when their mother didn't come home  on time sonomy went out to look for her  while genya was in charge of taking care  of the children the household was  attacked by a demon and everyone except  for genya was killed sanemy then showed  up and killed the demon but that demon  turned out to be their mother at first  genya was in shock and he didn't  understand what happened and he lashed  out at sonomy for killing their mother  genya would come to regret this later  when he actually came to terms with what  really happened but by then sunimi had  already abandoned him and dedicated his  life to hunting down demons sonemy  didn't even know that the demon slayers  existed and he didn't even know about  nietzsche and blades so he just used  whatever weapons he could find and he  would find demons trap them and then  burn them in the sunlight he was like a  one-man anti-demon vigilante squad and  his actions were so wild and reckless  that he later thought that he might have  been indirectly trying to end his own  life but he got lucky because he  possessed an extremely rare and special  blood type called marici this blood is  especially intoxicating to demons and it  distracts them and slows them down which  allowed sonemy to get the jump on them  during one of his demon hunts he met an  actual demonstrator named masatka kumeno  and he recruited tsunemi into the demon  slayer core sanomi and masachika became  friends and they both wanted to become  hashira together they defeated a lower  moon one but masatka died during that  battle and so only sanemy was able to go  on to become a hashida the death of  masachika made sanemy angry and he took  that anger out on oyakatasama  felt that as the leader of the  demonstrator core he was just giving out  orders while others were risking their  life on his behalf but to sunimi's  surprise oya katasama took the criticism  gracefully and he even apologized he  explained that his body is simply not  suited for fighting he tried to do it  before but he failed miserably because  of his physical limitations oya katasama  also expresses regret for the loss of  masachika and he knows that sanemy and  masajika were close like brothers oya  katasama's kind face reminds sanemy of  his mother before she became a demon and  the fact that oya katasama goes out of  his way to know and memorize the names  of every single demon sailor who fell in  battle gives sanomi a newfound respect  for the leader of the demon players the  loss of masachika and the will that his  friend left for tsunami also reminds  sanemi that he still has a brother out  there genya and although sanami  continues to be a loose cannon  throughout the series he definitely  calms down a bit and he stops being  completely reckless with his own life  and that is it the full backstory of  every hashira in the demon players story  these were of course the current hashida  that we meet at the beginning of the  story and although we know a bit about  the former hashira like shinjuro sakonji  and jigoro we don't know anything about  them before they became hashira so  because of that it's not really possible  to cover their backstories and of course  kanai's backstory is the same as  shinobus if you're looking for a video  to watch next check out my video that  breaks down the deaths of all the  